{c: Chords: the writer's own chart}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]You share my [Esus]grief, [E]You know my [Esus]hardship
[E]You came to [Esus]lift [E]my [B7sus]load
[E]You spoke of [Esus]love, [E]You offer [Esus]friendship
[E]Companions [Esus]on [E]the [B7sus]road
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Didn't [C#m]our hearts [G#7]burn in us,
[A]Epiphany, [F#7]while
[E]You spoke of Your [Esus]suffering,
[E]Spoke of Your [Esus]Father
[E]And of the [Esus]coming [E] [B7sus]power
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]You change my [Esus]heart, [E]You cleanse my [Esus]lips
[E]You came to [Esus]right [E]my [B7sus]wrongs
[E]Your voice is [Esus]sweet, [E]Your words are [Esus]flawless
[E]You circle [Esus]me [E]with [B7sus]songs
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[E]And the walls have [F#m7]ears and You [E/G#]sing with [F#m7]me
[E]And the clouds drop [F#m7]tears as You [E/G#]grieve with [F#m7]me
[E]Wanna I hear foot[F#m7]steps as You [E/G#]dance with [F#m7]me
[E]Window panes have [F#m7]scenes when You [E/G#]dream with [F#m7]me
You make me [A]clean
You make me [F#7]clean
You make me [A]clean
You make me [F#7]clean
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Ending}
Didn't [C#m]our hearts [G#7]burn in us, [A]Epiphany [F#7]
{end_of_verse}
